  Mattock is a twohanded weapon: fatal if cursed in Gehennom.  Also no
shield.  #twoweaponing blessed +7 Grayswandir and blessed +7 silver
saber is enjoyable: Slice and dice.  Just a couple of blessed +7 silver
sabers is worth it.  Both using the same skill saves a lot of skill
slots.

  The +10.5 average damage vs silver haters makes silver sabers the best
secondary weapon in Gehennom.  That lets #twoweaponing easily beat any
two-handed weapon, even artifact two-handed weapons.  (Because there are
no silver two-handed weapons.)

  #twoweaponing with Str:25 can be a good idea.  The Str:25 +6 damage
bonus applies to each weapon.  Be very careful at unskilled: -9 to-hit
bonus and -3 damage bonus per weapon.  (The DevTeam goes to sleep with a
smile on their face every night just from thinking about that.)

  #twoweaponing's main strength: Double damage bonuses (like strength,
and rings of increase damage) and an extra weapon to stick enchantments
on to.  (Kind of like wearing a shirt just to enchant it.)

  On the Ascension Run switch to a highly enchanted shield.  Number of
turns you should spend fighting with a melee weapon from then on: 0.
Wands of death, wands of polymorph, wand of teleport + jump, etc.

